# Directives

This page is the template-layer guide for structural control flow. The
contract is [Directives](/docs/reference/language/directives/).

**Verify:** `rocci inspect --ast FILE` shows `if` / `for` / `match` / `let` nodes.

Keep the opening `{` on the same logical header line. Parenthesize records in
headers so `{` is not the body opener: `@match ({ status, items }) {`.

## Conditional

```rocci
@if List.is_empty(items) {
    <p>Nothing yet.</p>
} @else {
    <p>{List.len(items).to_str()} items</p>
}
```

Missing `@else` becomes `Html.empty`. Use `@if` for a true/false condition.
Prefer `@match` when the input is a tag union or a small closed set.

## List

```rocci
@for item in items {
    <li id={"row-" ++ item.id.to_str()}>{item.label}</li>
}
```

One lowercase binder. Lowers to `List.map`. Give rows stable `id`s if a later
`@post:fragment` will morph them.

## Variants

```rocci
@match status {
    Idle => <p>Idle</p>
    Loading => <p>Loading</p>
    Failed(msg) => <p>{msg}</p>
}
```

An arm is an element, call, fragment, interpolation, or nested directive — not
bare text. Guards and `|` alternatives are ordinary Roc.

## Derived bindings

`@let name = expr` binds before render-producing items. Do not put `@fixture`
inside a component body.

**Related:** [Components](/docs/templates/components/),
[Directives reference](/docs/reference/language/directives/).
